.TH SUNMOON 1
.SH NAME
sunmoon \- two kinds of dithered flood fill
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/sunmoon
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I SunMoon
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/SunMoon.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A sun and a waxing moon.  The sun is flood-filled with a fixed
checkerboard of red and yellow, which is how a palette with no orange in
it produces one.  The moon is outlined twice \- its rim, and an arc that
is the terminator \- and the regions either side of that arc are filled
with a probability dither of light grey over black, at probabilities that
rise as the moon drifts left, so it waxes over the sixty-four frames.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/sunmoon.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
